    "content": "[Goal]\n\n- The statement \"where [[t]] is the minimum purity, [[p]], required\" is somewhat confusing; consider splitting the first sentence into two:\n\"You need to analyze <<the quality of [[n]] metals>>. Each metal has a purity [[p]] and requires a minimum purity [[t]] to <<pass the quality test>>.\"\n\n- For clarity, consider adding that [[p]] ≥ [[t]] is considered passing (e.g., from the sample statement above: \"... the quality test>> ([[p]] ≥ [[t]]).\"\n\n[Input]\n\n- (Just being nitpicky) Consider changing \"amount of metals\" to \"number of metals\".\n\n[Output]\n\n- Please state what players should do if none of the metals are selected. It may be difficult to tell if there should be a trailing newline character or not just by looking at the expected output.\n\nThank you :)",
